{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>לְהִתְגּוֹלֵל עָלֵינוּ</b> — from \"And Amasa was rolling (מִתְגּוֹלֵל) in blood\" (II Samuel 20:12), \"and a garment rolled (מְגוֹלָלָה) in blood\" (Isaiah 9:4) — like a man who turns from side to side upon his fellow." "<b>וּלְהִתְנַפֵּל עָלֵינוּ</b> — like a man who throws himself of his own will upon his fellow, his full height upon him. And Onkelos (Onkelos on Genesis 43:18) translated לְהִתְגּוֹלֵל as לְאִתְרַבְרָבָא עֲלַנָא — that he will surge against us like the sea's swelling upon its waves — and וּלְהִתְנַפֵּל as לְאִסְתַּקָּפָא, to lay upon us things that never were. For a matter that does not come to pass is called 'fallen (נוֹפֵל),' as in \"not one thing has fallen (נָפַל)\" (Joshua 23:14). And the translation of \"עֲלִילוֹת דְּבָרִים\" (Deuteronomy 22:14) is \"תַּסְקוּפֵּי מִלִּין,\" and so Jonathan translated \"תּוֹאֲנָה\" (Judges 14:4) as \"תּוּסְקְפָא.\"" "And the sense of <b>וְלָקַחַת אֹתָנוּ לַעֲבָדִים וְאֶת חֲמֹרֵינוּ</b> is that they feared for their donkeys, saying: behold, they will also take our donkeys together with their packs, and we will not be able to send grain home, and they will all die of the famine."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:44:40.286214346Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}